    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0854" n="826" xml:id="pg826"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> UNP files, lot 59 D 237, “Membership”</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Officer in Charge of General Assembly
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Taylor</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d580-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-07-16">July 16, 1952</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <item>Subject:</item>
                    <item>Circumvention or Overriding of Soviet Veto of Applications for United
                        Nations Membership</item>
                </list>
                <p>At a meeting of the Assistant Secretaries last week, during which it was
                    generally agreed that we should not acquiesce in a package proposal on
                    membership, Mr. Hickerson said that we would again look into the possibility of
                    circumventing or overriding the Soviet veto of membership applications.</p>
                <p>I hope that we can have a meeting some time this week to discuss this problem.
                    Attached is a paper on the subject to serve as a basis for our discussion.</p>


                <xi:include href="d580-a1.xml" xpointer="d580-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d580-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d580-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed to the Director of the Office of UN Political and Security Affairs
                    (Wainhouse) and the Assistant Legal Adviser for UN Affairs (Meeker).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
